-- Gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B, guidance for hand-gathering only): the three limbs are the routes to "may be a party in their own name".
-- The list has no "only", so when no limb holds the gathered answer is NOTHING.
-- src:358-363 | 1. The following may be parties to proceedings in their own name, whether as claimant, defendant, third party or in any other capacity: ( a ) a person
-- src:358-363 | who is 18 years of age or older but below 21 years of age and where section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies; ( b ) a person who is 21 years of age or
-- src:358-363 | older; ( c ) any entity with the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere.
@ref O 4 r 1 (src:358-363)
GIVEN person IS A `Kind of person`
      `section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity has the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 1 the person may be a party to proceedings in their own name` MEANS
    IF (`o 4 r 1(a) a person aged 18 or older but below 21 may be a party in their own name` person `section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`o 4 r 1(b) a person aged 21 or older may be a party in their own name` person EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`o 4 r 1(c) an entity with the capacity to sue or be sued may be a party in its own name` person `the entity has the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following may be parties" has no "only"

