DECLARE `o 4 r 3(6) the court to which an appeal is brought` IS ONE OF
    `o 4 r 3(6) an appeal to the Court of Appeal`
    `o 4 r 3(6) an appeal to the Appellate Division`
    `o 4 r 3(6) an appeal to the General Division`
    `o 4 r 3(6) an appeal to a District Court under Division 2 of Order 18`
    `o 4 r 3(6) not an appeal, or an appeal to another court`

DECLARE `o 4 r 3(6) a court named in the definition of Court` IS ONE OF
    `o 4 r 3(6)(a) the Court of Appeal`
    `o 4 r 3(6)(b) the Appellate Division`
    `o 4 r 3(6)(c) the General Division`
    `o 4 r 3(6)(d) a Family Court`
    `o 4 r 3(6)(e) a District Court`
    `o 4 r 3(6)(f) a Magistrate's Court`

-- Each head is asked on its own.  The heads overlap (an appeal from a General Division matter to the Court of Appeal is within both (a)(ii) and (c)(i)):
-- the text does not say which prevails, so the count below says how many heads hold, and a count above one is a finding.
-- src:398-421 | “Court” means — ( a ) the Court of Appeal, if the relevant matter or proceeding is — (i) any matter, proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)(
-- src:398-421 | a ); or (ii) any appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( c ), ( e ) or ( f ) to the Court of Appeal, in respect of which no permission has been given under
-- src:398-421 | paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below; ( b ) the Appellate Division, if the relevant matter or proceeding is — (i) any matter, proceeding or appeal
-- src:398-421 | mentioned in paragraph (5)( b ); or (ii) any appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( c ), ( e ) or ( f ) to the Appellate Division, in respect of which no
-- src:398-421 | permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below; ( c ) the General Division, if the matter or proceeding is — (i) any matter,
-- src:398-421 | proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( c ); or (ii) any appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( e ) or ( f ) to the General Division, in respect
-- src:398-421 | of which no permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below; ( d ) a Family Court, if the relevant matter or proceeding is any
-- src:398-421 | matter, proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( d ); ( e ) a District Court, if the relevant matter or proceeding is — (i) any matter,
-- src:398-421 | proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( e ); or (ii) any appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( f ) under Division 2 of Order 18, in respect of
-- src:398-421 | which no permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a Magistrate’s Court; or ( f ) a Magistrate’s Court, if the relevant matter or
-- src:398-421 | proceeding is any matter, proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( f );
@ref O 4 r 3(6) “Court” (src:398-421)
GIVEN court IS A `o 4 r 3(6) a court named in the definition of Court`
      category IS A `o 4 r 3(5) the relevant matter or proceeding`
      appeal IS A `o 4 r 3(6) the court to which an appeal is brought`
      `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 3(6) the Court is that court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(a) the Court of Appeal` THEN
        IF category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(a) a matter or proceeding commenced in, or an appeal under a written law from a tribunal to, the Court of Appeal`
           OR ((category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(c) a matter or proceeding commenced in the General Division and any appeal from it` OR category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(e) a matter or proceeding commenced in a District Court and any appeal from it` OR category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(f) a matter or proceeding commenced in a Magistrate's Court and any appeal from it`) AND appeal EQUALS `o 4 r 3(6) an appeal to the Court of Appeal` AND (NOT `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): head (a) of "“Court” means" and neither (i) nor (ii) holds
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(b) the Appellate Division` THEN
        IF category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(b) a matter or proceeding commenced in, or an appeal under a written law from a tribunal to, the Appellate Division`
           OR ((category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(c) a matter or proceeding commenced in the General Division and any appeal from it` OR category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(e) a matter or proceeding commenced in a District Court and any appeal from it` OR category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(f) a matter or proceeding commenced in a Magistrate's Court and any appeal from it`) AND appeal EQUALS `o 4 r 3(6) an appeal to the Appellate Division` AND (NOT `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): head (b) of "“Court” means" and neither (i) nor (ii) holds
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(c) the General Division` THEN
        IF category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(c) a matter or proceeding commenced in the General Division and any appeal from it`
           OR ((category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(e) a matter or proceeding commenced in a District Court and any appeal from it` OR category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(f) a matter or proceeding commenced in a Magistrate's Court and any appeal from it`) AND appeal EQUALS `o 4 r 3(6) an appeal to the General Division` AND (NOT `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): head (c) of "“Court” means" and neither (i) nor (ii) holds
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(d) a Family Court` THEN
        IF category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(d) a matter or proceeding commenced in a Family Court and any appeal from it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): head (d) of "“Court” means" does not hold
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(e) a District Court` THEN
        IF category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(e) a matter or proceeding commenced in a District Court and any appeal from it`
           OR (category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(f) a matter or proceeding commenced in a Magistrate's Court and any appeal from it` AND appeal EQUALS `o 4 r 3(6) an appeal to a District Court under Division 2 of Order 18` AND (NOT `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): head (e) of "“Court” means" and neither (i) nor (ii) holds
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(f) a Magistrate's Court` THEN
        IF category EQUALS `o 4 r 3(5)(f) a matter or proceeding commenced in a Magistrate's Court and any appeal from it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): head (f) of "“Court” means" does not hold

-- src:398-421 | “Court” means — ( a ) the Court of Appeal, if the relevant matter or proceeding is — (i) any matter, proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)(
-- src:398-421 | a ); or (ii) any appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( c ), ( e ) or ( f ) to the Court of Appeal, in respect of which no permission has been given under
-- src:398-421 | paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below; ( b ) the Appellate Division, if the relevant matter or proceeding is — (i) any matter, proceeding or appeal
-- src:398-421 | mentioned in paragraph (5)( b ); or (ii) any appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( c ), ( e ) or ( f ) to the Appellate Division, in respect of which no
-- src:398-421 | permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below; ( c ) the General Division, if the matter or proceeding is — (i) any matter,
-- src:398-421 | proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( c ); or (ii) any appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( e ) or ( f ) to the General Division, in respect
-- src:398-421 | of which no permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below; ( d ) a Family Court, if the relevant matter or proceeding is any
-- src:398-421 | matter, proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( d ); ( e ) a District Court, if the relevant matter or proceeding is — (i) any matter,
-- src:398-421 | proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( e ); or (ii) any appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( f ) under Division 2 of Order 18, in respect of
-- src:398-421 | which no permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a Magistrate’s Court; or ( f ) a Magistrate’s Court, if the relevant matter or
-- src:398-421 | proceeding is any matter, proceeding or appeal mentioned in paragraph (5)( f );
@ref O 4 r 3(6) “Court” (src:398-421)
GIVEN category IS A `o 4 r 3(5) the relevant matter or proceeding`
      appeal IS A `o 4 r 3(6) the court to which an appeal is brought`
      `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 4 r 3(6) the number of heads of the definition of Court that hold` MEANS
    (IF `o 4 r 3(6) the Court is that court` `o 4 r 3(6)(a) the Court of Appeal` category appeal `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF `o 4 r 3(6) the Court is that court` `o 4 r 3(6)(b) the Appellate Division` category appeal `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF `o 4 r 3(6) the Court is that court` `o 4 r 3(6)(c) the General Division` category appeal `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF `o 4 r 3(6) the Court is that court` `o 4 r 3(6)(d) a Family Court` category appeal `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF `o 4 r 3(6) the Court is that court` `o 4 r 3(6)(e) a District Court` category appeal `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF `o 4 r 3(6) the Court is that court` `o 4 r 3(6)(f) a Magistrate's Court` category appeal `permission has been given under paragraph (3) or (4) by a court below` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- src:422 | “limited liability partnership” means a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act;
@ref O 4 r 3(6) “limited liability partnership” (src:422)
GIVEN `it is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 3(6) a body is a limited liability partnership` MEANS
    IF `it is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“limited liability partnership” means a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act"

-- src:423 | “manager”, in relation to a limited liability partnership, has the meaning given by the Limited Liability Partnerships Act;
@ref O 4 r 3(6) “manager” (src:423)
GIVEN `the Limited Liability Partnerships Act gives the person the meaning of manager` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 3(6) a person is a manager of a limited liability partnership` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Limited Liability Partnerships Act gives the person the meaning of manager`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by the Limited Liability Partnerships Act

DECLARE `o 4 r 3(6) the body of which a person may be an officer` IS ONE OF
    `o 4 r 3(6)(a) a company or variable capital company`
    `o 4 r 3(6)(b) a limited liability partnership`
    `o 4 r 3(6)(c) an unincorporated association (other than a partnership or a registered trade union)`
    `o 4 r 3(6)(d) a registered trade union`
    `o 4 r 3(6) some other body`

-- src:424-431 | “officer” — ( a ) in relation to a company or variable capital company, means any director or secretary of the company or variable capital company, or
-- src:424-431 | a person employed in an executive capacity by the company or variable capital company; ( b ) in relation to a limited liability partnership, means any
-- src:424-431 | partner in or manager of the limited liability partnership; ( c ) in relation to an unincorporated association (other than a partnership or a
-- src:424-431 | registered trade union), means the president, the secretary, or any member of the committee of the unincorporated association; or ( d ) in relation to
-- src:424-431 | a registered trade union, has the meaning given by the Trade Unions Act;
@ref O 4 r 3(6) “officer” (src:424-431)
GIVEN body IS A `o 4 r 3(6) the body of which a person may be an officer`
      `the person is a director or secretary of the company or variable capital company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed in an executive capacity by the company or variable capital company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner in or manager of the limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the president, the secretary or a member of the committee of the unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Trade Unions Act gives the person the meaning of officer of the registered trade union` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 3(6) a person is an officer of the body` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(a) a company or variable capital company` THEN
        IF `the person is a director or secretary of the company or variable capital company` OR `the person is employed in an executive capacity by the company or variable capital company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“officer” — (a) in relation to a company or variable capital company, means any director or secretary ..., or a person employed in an executive capacity"
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(b) a limited liability partnership` THEN
        IF `the person is a partner in or manager of the limited liability partnership`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to a limited liability partnership, means any partner in or manager of the limited liability partnership"
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(c) an unincorporated association (other than a partnership or a registered trade union)` THEN
        IF `the person is the president, the secretary or a member of the committee of the unincorporated association`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) in relation to an unincorporated association ..., means the president, the secretary, or any member of the committee"
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6)(d) a registered trade union` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Trade Unions Act gives the person the meaning of officer of the registered trade union`
        WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(d) in relation to a registered trade union, has the meaning given by the Trade Unions Act"
    WHEN `o 4 r 3(6) some other body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the definition of "officer" is "in relation to" the four bodies it names

-- src:432 | “partner”, in relation to a limited liability partnership, has the meaning given by the Limited Liability Partnerships Act;
@ref O 4 r 3(6) “partner” (src:432)
GIVEN `the Limited Liability Partnerships Act gives the person the meaning of partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 3(6) a person is a partner of a limited liability partnership` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Limited Liability Partnerships Act gives the person the meaning of partner`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by the Limited Liability Partnerships Act

-- src:433 | “registered trade union” has the meaning given by the Trade Unions Act;
@ref O 4 r 3(6) “registered trade union” (src:433)
GIVEN `the Trade Unions Act gives the body the meaning of registered trade union` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 3(6) a body is a registered trade union` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Trade Unions Act gives the body the meaning of registered trade union`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by the Trade Unions Act

-- src:434 | “variable capital company” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018.
@ref O 4 r 3(6) “variable capital company” (src:434)
GIVEN `section 2(1) of the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018 gives the body the meaning of variable capital company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 3(6) a body is a variable capital company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `section 2(1) of the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018 gives the body the meaning of variable capital company`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by section 2(1) of the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 4, Rule 4 -- representation of estates`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:436 | 4. —(1) Where any defendant has died but a cause of action against him or her survives and no grant of probate or letters of administration has been
-- src:436 | made, the action may be brought against the estate of the deceased which is to be described as “personal representatives of (defendant’s name)
-- src:436 | deceased”.
@ref O 4 r 4(1) (src:436)
GIVEN `a defendant has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cause of action against the defendant survives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 4(1) the action may be brought against the estate of the deceased` MEANS
    IF `a defendant has died` AND `a cause of action against the defendant survives` AND (NOT `a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any defendant has died but a cause of action against him or her survives and no grant of probate or letters of administration has been made"

-- src:436 | 4. —(1) Where any defendant has died but a cause of action against him or her survives and no grant of probate or letters of administration has been
-- src:436 | made, the action may be brought against the estate of the deceased which is to be described as “personal representatives of (defendant’s name)
-- src:436 | deceased”.
@ref O 4 r 4(1) (src:436)
GIVEN `the defendant's name` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`o 4 r 4(1) the description of the estate of the deceased` MEANS
    CONCAT "personal representatives of ", `the defendant's name`, " deceased"

-- src:436-441 | (2) In any action brought against the estate of a deceased person — ( a ) the claimant must, during the period of validity for service of the
-- src:436-441 | originating claim or originating application, apply to the Court for — (i) an order appointing a person to represent the deceased’s estate for the
-- src:436-441 | purpose of the proceedings; or (ii) if a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made — an order that the personal representative of
-- src:436-441 | the deceased be made a party to the proceedings, and in either case for an order that the proceedings be carried on against the person appointed or
-- src:436-441 | (as the case may be) against the personal representative, as if he or she had been substituted for the estate; and
@ref O 4 r 4(2)(a) (src:436-441)
GIVEN `the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 4(2)(a) the claimant must apply to the Court for an order during the period of validity for service` MEANS
    IF `the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "In any action brought against the estate of a deceased person"

DECLARE `o 4 r 4(2)(a) the order applied for` IS ONE OF
    `o 4 r 4(2)(a)(i) an order appointing a person to represent the deceased's estate for the purpose of the proceedings`
    `o 4 r 4(2)(a)(ii) an order that the personal representative of the deceased be made a party to the proceedings`
    `o 4 r 4(2)(a) some other order`

-- src:436-441 | (2) In any action brought against the estate of a deceased person — ( a ) the claimant must, during the period of validity for service of the
-- src:436-441 | originating claim or originating application, apply to the Court for — (i) an order appointing a person to represent the deceased’s estate for the
-- src:436-441 | purpose of the proceedings; or (ii) if a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made — an order that the personal representative of
-- src:436-441 | the deceased be made a party to the proceedings, and in either case for an order that the proceedings be carried on against the person appointed or
-- src:436-441 | (as the case may be) against the personal representative, as if he or she had been substituted for the estate; and
@ref O 4 r 4(2)(a) (src:436-441)
GIVEN order IS A `o 4 r 4(2)(a) the order applied for`
      `a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 4(2)(a) the claimant may apply for that order` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `o 4 r 4(2)(a)(i) an order appointing a person to represent the deceased's estate for the purpose of the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 4 r 4(2)(a)(ii) an order that the personal representative of the deceased be made a party to the proceedings` THEN
        IF `a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made — an order that the personal representative of the deceased be made a party to the proceedings"
    WHEN `o 4 r 4(2)(a) some other order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sub-paragraph names two orders and has no "only"

-- The application must be made "during the period of validity for service of the originating claim or originating application": Order 6, Rule 3.
-- src:436-441 | (2) In any action brought against the estate of a deceased person — ( a ) the claimant must, during the period of validity for service of the
-- src:436-441 | originating claim or originating application, apply to the Court for — (i) an order appointing a person to represent the deceased’s estate for the
-- src:436-441 | purpose of the proceedings; or (ii) if a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made — an order that the personal representative of
-- src:436-441 | the deceased be made a party to the proceedings, and in either case for an order that the proceedings be carried on against the person appointed or
-- src:436-441 | (as the case may be) against the personal representative, as if he or she had been substituted for the estate; and
@ref O 4 r 4(2)(a) (src:436-441)
GIVEN `the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant applies for an order appointing a person to represent the estate or, if a grant has been made, an order that the personal representative be made a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant also applies for an order that the proceedings be carried on against the person appointed or the personal representative as if substituted for the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originating claim or originating application is valid for service on the day of the application` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 4(2)(a) the claimant has applied to the Court as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "In any action brought against the estate of a deceased person"
        IF (NOT `the claimant applies for an order appointing a person to represent the estate or, if a grant has been made, an order that the personal representative be made a party`)
           OR (NOT `the claimant also applies for an order that the proceedings be carried on against the person appointed or the personal representative as if substituted for the estate`)
           OR `the originating claim or originating application is valid for service on the day of the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant must, during the period of validity for service of the originating claim or originating application, apply to the Court for" the orders
        IF `the originating claim or originating application is valid for service on the day of the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the application was made during the period of validity is not decided on these facts

-- src:443 | the Court may, at any stage of the proceedings and on any terms that the Court thinks just and either of its own motion or on application, make any
-- src:443 | order mentioned in sub‑paragraph ( a ) and allow amendments (if any) to be made, and make any other order that the Court thinks necessary in order to
-- src:443 | ensure that all matters in dispute in the proceedings may be effectually and completely determined and adjudicated upon.
@ref O 4 r 4(2)(b) (src:443)
GIVEN `the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is one mentioned in sub-paragraph (a), an amendment, or another order the Court thinks necessary in order to ensure that all matters in dispute may be effectually and completely determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 4(2)(b) the Court may make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "In any action brought against the estate of a deceased person"
        IF `the order is one mentioned in sub-paragraph (a), an amendment, or another order the Court thinks necessary in order to ensure that all matters in dispute may be effectually and completely determined`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph names the orders the Court may make and has no "only"

-- src:444 | (3) Where the Public Trustee has been appointed by an order under paragraph (2) to represent the deceased’s estate, the originating claim or
-- src:444 | originating application for the action must be served on the Public Trustee, whose appointment is limited to accepting service of the originating
-- src:444 | claim or originating application unless the Public Trustee consents to take further steps in the proceedings on behalf of the estate of the defendant.
@ref O 4 r 4(3) (src:444)
GIVEN `the Public Trustee has been appointed by an order under paragraph (2) to represent the deceased's estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 4(3) the originating claim or originating application must be served on the Public Trustee` MEANS
    IF `the Public Trustee has been appointed by an order under paragraph (2) to represent the deceased's estate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Public Trustee has been appointed by an order under paragraph (2) to represent the deceased’s estate"

-- src:444 | (3) Where the Public Trustee has been appointed by an order under paragraph (2) to represent the deceased’s estate, the originating claim or
-- src:444 | originating application for the action must be served on the Public Trustee, whose appointment is limited to accepting service of the originating
-- src:444 | claim or originating application unless the Public Trustee consents to take further steps in the proceedings on behalf of the estate of the defendant.
@ref O 4 r 4(3) (src:444)
GIVEN `the Public Trustee has been appointed by an order under paragraph (2) to represent the deceased's estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Public Trustee consents to take further steps in the proceedings on behalf of the estate of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 4(3) the Public Trustee's appointment extends beyond accepting service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Public Trustee has been appointed by an order under paragraph (2) to represent the deceased's estate`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Public Trustee has been appointed by an order under paragraph (2) to represent the deceased’s estate"
        IF `the Public Trustee consents to take further steps in the proceedings on behalf of the estate of the defendant`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless the Public Trustee consents to take further steps" lifts the limit and does not say how far the appointment then reaches
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whose appointment is limited to accepting service of the originating claim or originating application"

-- src:445 | (4) Where no grant of probate or letters of administration has been made, any judgment or order given or made in the action binds the estate to the
-- src:445 | same extent as if a grant had been made and a personal representative of the deceased had been a party to the action.
@ref O 4 r 4(4) (src:445)
GIVEN `the action is brought against the estate under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 4(4) the judgment or order binds the estate as if a grant had been made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is brought against the estate under paragraph (1)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the effect is of "any judgment or order given or made in the action" brought against the estate
        IF `a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where no grant of probate or letters of administration has been made"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 4, Rules 5 to 7 -- death or bankruptcy; representative proceedings; declarations`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:447 | 5. —(1) Where a party to an action dies or becomes bankrupt after the action has been commenced but the cause of action survives, the action does not
-- src:447 | terminate by reason of the death or bankruptcy.
@ref O 4 r 5(1) (src:447)
GIVEN `a party to an action dies or becomes bankrupt after the action has been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause of action survives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 5(1) the action continues despite the death or bankruptcy` MEANS
    IF `a party to an action dies or becomes bankrupt after the action has been commenced` AND `the cause of action survives`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party to an action dies or becomes bankrupt after the action has been commenced but the cause of action survives" (the provision gives continuation only in that case)

-- src:447 | (2) At the case conference, the Court must give directions for the further conduct of the action.
@ref O 4 r 5(2) (src:447)
GIVEN `a party to an action has died or become bankrupt after the action was commenced and the cause of action survives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 5(2) the Court must give directions at the case conference for the further conduct of the action` MEANS
    IF `a party to an action has died or become bankrupt after the action was commenced and the cause of action survives`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) follows paragraph (1) and reaches the action that paragraph (1) keeps alive

-- src:449 | 6. —(1) Where numerous persons have a common interest in any proceedings, such persons may sue or be sued as a group with one or more of them
-- src:449 | representing the group.
@ref O 4 r 6(1) (src:449)
GIVEN `numerous persons have a common interest in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 6(1) the persons may sue or be sued as a group with one or more representing the group` MEANS
    IF `numerous persons have a common interest in the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where numerous persons have a common interest in any proceedings"

-- src:449 | (2) Where a group of persons is suing under this Rule, all members in the group must give their consent in writing to the representative to represent
-- src:449 | all of them in the action and they must be included in a list of claimants attached to the originating claim or the originating application.
@ref O 4 r 6(2) (src:449)
GIVEN `a group of persons is suing under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 6(2) all members of the group must consent in writing and be included in a list of claimants` MEANS
    IF `a group of persons is suing under this Rule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a group of persons is suing under this Rule"

-- src:449 | (2) Where a group of persons is suing under this Rule, all members in the group must give their consent in writing to the representative to represent
-- src:449 | all of them in the action and they must be included in a list of claimants attached to the originating claim or the originating application.
@ref O 4 r 6(2) (src:449)
GIVEN `a group of persons is suing under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all members in the group have given their consent in writing to the representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all members are included in a list of claimants attached to the originating claim or the originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 6(2) the group has complied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a group of persons is suing under this Rule`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "Where a group of persons is suing under this Rule"
        IF `all members in the group have given their consent in writing to the representative` AND `all members are included in a list of claimants attached to the originating claim or the originating application`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all members in the group must give their consent in writing ... and they must be included in a list of claimants attached to the originating claim or the originating application"

-- src:450 | (3) Where a group of persons is being sued under this Rule, the Court may appoint one or more of them as representative to represent those in the
-- src:450 | group who have given their consent in writing to the representative in the action and they must be included in a list of defendants attached to the
-- src:450 | order of Court.
@ref O 4 r 6(3) (src:450)
GIVEN `a group of persons is being sued under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 6(3) the Court may appoint one or more of them as representative` MEANS
