-- An "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): the deeming lasts until the final conclusion of the action in the Court.
-- JUST TRUE = the deeming has not yet ended; JUST FALSE = the action has reached its final conclusion.  It never says the solicitor is still acting.
-- src:456 | (2) Unless notice is given according to this Rule, a solicitor who is appointed by a party at any stage of an action is deemed to be acting for the
-- src:456 | party in the action until the final conclusion of the action in the Court, and his or her business address is deemed to be the address for service of
-- src:456 | all documents in the action until such conclusion.
@ref O 4 r 8(2) (src:456)
GIVEN `the solicitor is appointed by a party at any stage of an action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice is given according to this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action has reached its final conclusion in the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 8(2) the deeming of the solicitor cannot yet end` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the solicitor is appointed by a party at any stage of an action`) OR `notice is given according to this Rule`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming applies to a solicitor appointed at any stage "Unless notice is given according to this Rule"
        IF `the action has reached its final conclusion in the Court`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the final conclusion of the action in the Court" (the bar has lifted)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

