-- Paragraph (6): the notice takes effect from the time of service.  The time asked about is compared with the time of service (day, then minutes after midnight).
-- src:460 | (6) Notice given under this Rule takes effect from the time of service of the notice and does not affect the rights of the solicitor and the party who
-- src:460 | appointed the solicitor as between themselves.
@ref O 4 r 8(6) (src:460)
GIVEN `the notice is given under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time of service of the notice` IS A Moment
      `the time in question` IS A Moment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 8(6) the notice has taken effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the notice is given under this Rule`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is of "Notice given under this Rule"
        IF `the time in question`'s `day of the moment` GREATER THAN `the time of service of the notice`'s `day of the moment`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the time in question`'s `day of the moment` EQUALS `the time of service of the notice`'s `day of the moment` AND `the time in question`'s `minutes after midnight` AT LEAST `the time of service of the notice`'s `minutes after midnight`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "takes effect from the time of service of the notice"

