-- src:466 | 9. —(1) Where a solicitor who has acted for a party in a cause or matter has ceased so to act and the party has not given notice of change in
-- src:466 | accordance with Rule 8(3), or notice of intention to act in person in accordance with Rule 8(4), the solicitor may apply to the Court for an order
-- src:466 | declaring that the solicitor has ceased to be the solicitor acting for the party in the cause or matter, and the Court may make an order accordingly,
-- src:466 | but until the solicitor serves on every party to the cause or matter (not being a party in default as to the filing of a notice of intention to
-- src:466 | contest or not contest) a copy of the order and files a notice in Form 5 of his or her having ceased to act as solicitor for the party, the solicitor
-- src:466 | is, subject to Rule 8, considered the solicitor of the party till the final conclusion of the cause or matter.
@ref O 4 r 9(1) (src:466)
GIVEN `a solicitor who has acted for a party in a cause or matter has ceased so to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has not given notice of change in accordance with Rule 8(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has not given notice of intention to act in person in accordance with Rule 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the solicitor has served a copy of the order on every party to the cause or matter (not being a party in default as to the filing of a notice of intention to contest or not contest)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the solicitor has filed a notice in Form 5 of having ceased to act as solicitor for the party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause or matter has reached its final conclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 8 otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 9(1) the solicitor is still considered the solicitor of the party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a solicitor who has acted for a party in a cause or matter has ceased so to act` AND `the party has not given notice of change in accordance with Rule 8(3)` AND `the party has not given notice of intention to act in person in accordance with Rule 8(4)`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a solicitor who has acted for a party in a cause or matter has ceased so to act and the party has not given notice" ("where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); the same condition already answers JUST FALSE in `o 4 r 9(1) the solicitor may apply to the Court for an order declaring that the solicitor has ceased to act`)
        IF `Rule 8 otherwise provides`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to Rule 8"
        IF (`the solicitor has served a copy of the order on every party to the cause or matter (not being a party in default as to the filing of a notice of intention to contest or not contest)` AND `the solicitor has filed a notice in Form 5 of having ceased to act as solicitor for the party`) OR `the cause or matter has reached its final conclusion`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the solicitor serves ... a copy of the order and files a notice in Form 5 ... till the final conclusion of the cause or matter" (the bar has lifted)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Which Form the notice of having ceased to act is in: the text says Form 5 (the "until" bar above takes the fact that it was filed as an input).
-- src:466 | 9. —(1) Where a solicitor who has acted for a party in a cause or matter has ceased so to act and the party has not given notice of change in
-- src:466 | accordance with Rule 8(3), or notice of intention to act in person in accordance with Rule 8(4), the solicitor may apply to the Court for an order
-- src:466 | declaring that the solicitor has ceased to be the solicitor acting for the party in the cause or matter, and the Court may make an order accordingly,
-- src:466 | but until the solicitor serves on every party to the cause or matter (not being a party in default as to the filing of a notice of intention to
-- src:466 | contest or not contest) a copy of the order and files a notice in Form 5 of his or her having ceased to act as solicitor for the party, the solicitor
-- src:466 | is, subject to Rule 8, considered the solicitor of the party till the final conclusion of the cause or matter.
@ref O 4 r 9(1) (src:466)
GIVEN `the Form number used` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 9(1) the notice of having ceased to act is in the Form the text names` MEANS
    IF `the Form number used` EQUALS "5"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "files a notice in Form 5 of his or her having ceased to act as solicitor for the party"

-- src:466 | (2) An application for an order under this Rule must be made by summons in Form 6 and the summons must, unless the Court otherwise directs, be served
-- src:466 | on the party for whom the solicitor acted.
@ref O 4 r 9(2) (src:466)
GIVEN `the application is for an order under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Form number used` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 9(2) the application is made by summons in Form 6` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is for an order under this Rule`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for "An application for an order under this Rule"
        IF `the application is made by summons` AND `the Form number used` EQUALS "6"
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made by summons in Form 6"

-- src:466 | (2) An application for an order under this Rule must be made by summons in Form 6 and the summons must, unless the Court otherwise directs, be served
-- src:466 | on the party for whom the solicitor acted.
@ref O 4 r 9(2) (src:466)
GIVEN `the application is for an order under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is served on the party for whom the solicitor acted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 9(2) the summons has been served on the party for whom the solicitor acted as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is for an order under this Rule`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for "An application for an order under this Rule"
        IF `the Court otherwise directs`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless the Court otherwise directs" lifts the requirement and does not say what then applies
        IF `the summons is served on the party for whom the solicitor acted`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the summons must, unless the Court otherwise directs, be served on the party for whom the solicitor acted"

-- src:467 | (3) The application mentioned in paragraph (2) must be supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application.
@ref O 4 r 9(3) (src:467)
GIVEN `it is the application mentioned in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 9(3) the application is supported by an affidavit as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is the application mentioned in paragraph (2)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for "The application mentioned in paragraph (2)"
        IF `it is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application"

-- src:468 | (4) An order in Form 7 made under this Rule does not affect the rights of the solicitor and the party for whom he or she acted as between themselves.
@ref O 4 r 9(4) (src:468)
GIVEN `the order is made under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Form number used` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 9(4) the order affects the rights of the solicitor and the party as between themselves` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under this Rule` AND `the Form number used` EQUALS "7"
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order in Form 7 made under this Rule does not affect the rights of the solicitor and the party for whom he or she acted as between themselves"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative is of "An order in Form 7 made under this Rule"

-- src:469 | (5) Despite anything in paragraph (1), where the legal aid certificate of an assisted person within the meaning of the Legal Aid and Advice Act is
-- src:469 | revoked or discharged, the solicitor who acted for the assisted person ceases to be the solicitor acting in the cause or matter; and if the assisted
-- src:469 | person whose certificate has been revoked or discharged desires to proceed with the cause or matter without legal aid and appoints that solicitor or
-- src:469 | another solicitor to act on his or her behalf, Rule 8(1) applies as if that party had previously sued or defended in person.
@ref O 4 r 9(5) (src:469)
GIVEN `the legal aid certificate of an assisted person within the meaning of the Legal Aid and Advice Act is revoked or discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 9(5) the solicitor who acted for the assisted person ceases to be the solicitor acting` MEANS
    IF `the legal aid certificate of an assisted person within the meaning of the Legal Aid and Advice Act is revoked or discharged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the legal aid certificate of an assisted person within the meaning of the Legal Aid and Advice Act is revoked or discharged"

-- src:469 | (5) Despite anything in paragraph (1), where the legal aid certificate of an assisted person within the meaning of the Legal Aid and Advice Act is
-- src:469 | revoked or discharged, the solicitor who acted for the assisted person ceases to be the solicitor acting in the cause or matter; and if the assisted
-- src:469 | person whose certificate has been revoked or discharged desires to proceed with the cause or matter without legal aid and appoints that solicitor or
-- src:469 | another solicitor to act on his or her behalf, Rule 8(1) applies as if that party had previously sued or defended in person.
@ref O 4 r 9(5) (src:469)
GIVEN `the legal aid certificate of an assisted person within the meaning of the Legal Aid and Advice Act is revoked or discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assisted person desires to proceed with the cause or matter without legal aid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assisted person appoints that solicitor or another solicitor to act on the assisted person's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 4 r 9(5) Rule 8(1) applies as if the party had previously sued or defended in person` MEANS
    IF `the legal aid certificate of an assisted person within the meaning of the Legal Aid and Advice Act is revoked or discharged` AND `the assisted person desires to proceed with the cause or matter without legal aid` AND `the assisted person appoints that solicitor or another solicitor to act on the assisted person's behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the assisted person whose certificate has been revoked or discharged desires to proceed with the cause or matter without legal aid and appoints that solicitor or another solicitor to act on his or her behalf"

